The document is titled “ALLOCATION LETTER” and is dated 16thAugust, 20223. It is directed to Bob-Ogbonnaugochinyeramarilin at his residence located in WuseZone 6, Federal Capital Territory (FCT) Abuja. The letter confirms that upon full payment, permission has been granted for the assignment of shop space designated as COLDROOM 38 within the WuyeUltra-Modern (BOT)Market subject to adherence to the following stipulations:

a. Completion of a formal sales agreement between the developer and the shop purchaser;
b. Prohibition against any structural modifications or additional constructions without prior written consent from All Purpose SheltersLimited;
c. Non-refundability of the deposit amount already paid;
d. Prohibition of individual standby generators within the premises of the market;
e. Restriction on printing activities within the market boundaries;
f. Obligation for all shop proprietors to pay all statutory charges, levies, and taxes imposed by relevant authorities;
g. Imposition of a penalty rate of 2% per month on any delayed payments related to statutory fees;
h. Requirement for all shop owners to promptly settle all service charges due to All Purpose SheltersLimited, including maintenance fees, security levies, generator services, and waste management costs.

